Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The previous strategy opened constrained mode based on local token shape
// heuristics (digits, operators, "<"), which caused it to enter `<< ... >>`
// almost immediately and then get stuck producing malformed arithmetic spans.
// To fix the evaluation failures, this strategy becomes conservative:
//
// 1. Outside constrained mode, it stays fully unconstrained and simply appends
//    normal model tokens.
// 2. The only time it opens a constrained span is when the model itself emits
//    the exact delimiter token "<<".
// 3. Inside constrained mode, it never improvises delimiter handling from raw
//    sampled text. It either closes only when the parser says the constrained
//    prefix is complete, or appends a parser-approved token chosen by the
//    constrained helper.
// 4. If the constrained prefix becomes a dead end, it rolls back to a valid
//    prefix and then either closes if complete or continues with a constrained
//    step.
//
// This directly addresses the observed problems: no premature entry into
// constrained mode, no malformed content from heuristic opening, and no closing
// on a guessed ">>" token. The method still uses only verified helpers and
// keeps a simple one-step-per-iteration accounting discipline.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the outside branch we either remain outside after
// appending an unconstrained token, making the implication vacuous, or we open
// only through OpenConstrainedSpan, which establishes a valid empty constrained
// prefix. In the inside-complete branch, CloseConstrainedSpan exits constrained
// mode so the implication is vacuous. In the rollback branch,
// RollbackToValidPrefix returns a valid prefix; if that rolled prefix is
// complete we close, otherwise we stay inside with that valid prefix. In the
// normal inside branch, ConstrainedStep provides a parser-valid next token and
// AppendConstrainedToken preserves validity.
//
// suffix: Outside constrained mode the implication is vacuous. Opening through
// OpenConstrainedSpan establishes the helper-maintained relationship between the
// generated suffix and the constrained prefix. Closing makes the implication
// vacuous again. In rollback, generated is rewritten as its old unconstrained
// prefix plus the rolled constrained prefix, so the suffix equals the new
// currentConstrainedOut. In the append branch, AppendConstrainedToken extends
// generated and currentConstrainedOut in lockstep, preserving the suffix
// equality.
//
// cost: Each iteration performs at most one cost-bumping helper call:
// UnconstrainedStep, OpenConstrainedSpan, CloseConstrainedSpan, or
// ConstrainedStep. Query helpers and AppendConstrainedToken do not bump cost.
// After the branch's bumping helper finishes, the loop increments steps exactly
// once, so helpers.cost <= steps is preserved on the back-edge and at breaks.
//
// progress: In the outside branch, UnconstrainedStep samples at most one token;
// if we append it, generated grows by one while steps also grows by one, and if
// it is "<<" we instead use OpenConstrainedSpan which appends only the opening
// delimiter token. CloseConstrainedSpan appends only the closing delimiter
// token. Rollback may shorten generated before any later append or close, which
